+# Bug Assessment: Deleting products breaks carts and historical orders
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Merchants deleting a discontinued product currently break carts containing it and order reads containing it. The requested behavior is to remove deleted products from carts while preserving usable totals and checkout, reject newly added deleted products with 404, and preserve immutable order-line snapshots (SKU, name, quantity, price, subtotal and totals) across all listed order APIs and status updates. Deleted products must also return 404 from `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` without affecting other products.
+
+## Symptom
+
+Product deletion removes the product record needed by cart population, cart calculation, checkout, and order response enrichment. Existing carts/orders therefore fail or become inaccessible instead of retaining cart usability and historical order data.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a product, add it to a cart, and place an order containing it.
+2. Delete the product through `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}`.
+3. Read and mutate the cart, attempt checkout, read the order through private and authenticated endpoints, change order status, and request `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`.
+4. Verify the cart excludes the deleted line and recalculates totals, the order preserves its purchased line and totals, new additions receive 404, and the deleted product endpoint receives 404. Exact fixture/authentication setup is [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: environment-specific].
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/ProductServiceImpl.java:215-243` — hard-deletes the product and its related catalog data, so later SKU lookups return null.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java:226-315` — repopulates each cart item by SKU, marks missing products obsolete, and marks the whole cart obsolete; this currently causes deleted-product carts to be discarded rather than filtered.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java:96-190` — dereferences `item.getProduct()` and calculates the API representation from populated items, so missing products can fail conversion.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java:49-112` — correctly starts from persisted order-line fields but conditionally enriches from the current product; historical output must remain valid when that enrichment returns null.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java:52-126` — deprecated order conversion has the same nullable product-enrichment path and must not require the deleted catalog entity.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartModelPopulator.java:180-218` — adds cart items by SKU and currently throws a generic exception for a missing product; the API boundary should expose 404.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductApi.java:165-168` and `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v2/product/ProductApiV2.java` — product deletion and public SKU lookup endpoints whose post-delete behavior must remain 404.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+The product entity is used as a live foreign-data source for carts and order response decoration even though carts and orders store SKU, name, quantity and price snapshots. Product deletion therefore leaves persisted dependent rows pointing at an unavailable catalog entity; cart loading treats the missing line as a cart-level obsolete condition, while order mapping can fail or omit required historical context. Confidence: high.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Make cart loading prune only line items whose SKU no longer resolves, delete their orphaned cart-item/attribute rows safely, and retain the cart even when it becomes empty. Recalculate cart quantity, subtotal and total from the remaining lines and ensure checkout uses only those lines. Keep product creation/addition validation on the missing-SKU path and map it to the API's 404 exception. Ensure the cart data populator tolerates an empty cart and never dereferences a missing product.
+
+Make order response mapping rely on persisted `OrderProduct` snapshot fields for SKU, name, quantity, price and subtotal, treating current-product/image enrichment as optional. Preserve order totals and status operations. Keep hard deletion so normal product/SKU lookup naturally returns 404, and ensure deletion cleanup does not cascade into order-product history or unrelated products.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartModelPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java`
+- Relevant cart, order and product API integration tests under `sm-shop/src/test` and service tests under `sm-core/src/test`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+
+- Integration coverage for deleting a product from a mixed cart and an only-item cart, then reading, updating, multi-updating and checking out; verify totals and that adding the deleted SKU returns 404.
+- Integration coverage for all four order read endpoints and order status update after product deletion, asserting the persisted line snapshot and unchanged totals.
+- Coverage that the deleted SKU returns 404 from v2 product lookup and another product remains unaffected.
+- Service/populator unit coverage for pruning missing cart products and mapping historical order lines without a live product.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Cart-item orphan cleanup must respect JPA cascades and avoid deleting the cart or any order data.
+- Existing carts with all products deleted must remain readable and checkoutable as zero-value carts; obsolete-cart cleanup semantics may need narrowing.
+- The 404 mapping must use the existing API exception conventions rather than changing unrelated error responses.
+- Product enrichment such as images and live descriptions is unavailable after deletion; historical fields must come only from the order snapshot.
+- Broad integration tests may require the application/database fixture and authentication setup, so local verification may be limited.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact local integration-test database and authentication setup]
