+# Bug Fix: Deleting products breaks carts and historical orders
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Cart hydration now removes only lines whose SKU no longer resolves, cleans their dependent cart attributes/items, and keeps the cart available even when no products remain. Missing products added through the cart facade now use the existing 404 exception path; empty cart representations are explicitly populated.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` | modified | Prune deleted-product lines, clean orphan attributes, retain the cart, and clear obsolete state. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java` | modified | Always set the cart item list, including an empty list. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Return `ResourceNotFoundException` for missing SKU additions. |
+
+## Diff Highlights
+
+- Missing cart products are collected, removed from the cart line-item set, and deleted with their cart attributes before the cart is updated.
+- Cart-level `obsolete` is no longer set merely because a product was deleted; an empty cart can therefore be read and recalculated.
+- The cart API’s SKU creation path now raises the project’s 404 exception rather than a generic exception.
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- No new test source was added; existing core and cart API tests were run. The repository lacks a delete-product/order-history regression fixture, so the full ticket scenario remains a follow-up test opportunity.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core -Dtest=ShoppingCartTest test` → blocked by direct-module remote sibling dependency resolution (`spring-releases` unauthorized).
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=ShoppingCartTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed; 1 test, 0 failures.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-shop -am -DskipTests test-compile` → passed.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-shop -am -Dtest=ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed; 7 tests, 0 failures.
+- Manual checks: `git diff --check` passed; no end-to-end deleted-product/order fixture was available.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The assessment proposed changes to order mappers and new regression tests. Inspection showed both current order mappers already populate SKU, name, quantity, price and subtotal from persisted `OrderProduct` fields and treat live-product enrichment as optional, so no order mapper change was necessary. No new tests were added because the existing fixture set has no product-delete/order-history scenario; this is documented as a residual verification gap.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add an integration fixture covering product deletion followed by mixed/empty cart reads, cart mutation, checkout, all order read endpoints, status update, and v2 SKU lookup.
